    <h1>Five backends, one incremental compiler: Oreslang's next architecture</h1>
    <LogPrompt prompt={prompt} label="The engineering question" headingTag="div" />
    <div class="log-entry-meta"><span>Authored by <strong>Alex Mills</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time></div>
    <p class="log-entry-intro">Wasm is important, but the bigger opportunity is a shared, verified semantic core with function-level incremental compilation. Change one function; rebuild only what truly depends on it—without invalidating ownership proofs or compromising AOT.</p>
  </header>

